      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "© 2015 Wiley Periodicals, Inc.",
        "AbstractText": "Unfractionated heparin (UFH) and low molecular weight heparin (LMWH) are associated with side effects including hematomas, skin necrosis, contact dermatitis, and urticaria. We present a patient awaiting bypass surgery who developed bullous hemorrhagic dermatosis following LMWH."
